~ core.test.report — the harness and the reporter Quilon ships. Import with
~ `<< core.test.report`; it pulls in `core.test`, so a suite needs nothing else.
~ Reference: docs/corelib/test.md.
~
~   describe(name, body)  group of cases (nestable). `body` is a `() -> $` closure.
~   it(name, body)        one case, reported once it has run.
~
~   describe("trimming", () => <
~     it("drops both ends", () => expect("  x  ".trim(), equals("x")))
~   >)
~
~ Output is decided here, not in the compiler, and nothing in this file is privileged: a
~ suite that imports `core.test` alone and defines its own `describe`, `it`, `reportSuite`,
~ `reportCase` and `reportSummary` replaces the whole of it. `quilon test` binds
~ `reportSummary` by name, so whichever definition is in scope is the one that ends the run
~ and says whether it passed.
<< core.io
<< core.test

~ Two spaces per level of `describe` nesting.
>> indent = (depth :: Num) -> Text => "  ".repeat(depth)

~ The two colors the report uses, each plain when stdout is not a terminal that wants
~ color. Not folded into one `paint(code, text)` helper: a module's non-exported names are
~ not linked into a program, and the shared body is not worth a third exported name.
>> green = (text :: Text) -> Text =>
  __color_enabled(stdout) ? "\e[32m`text`\e[0m" : text

>> red = (text :: Text) -> Text =>
  __color_enabled(stdout) ? "\e[31m`text`\e[0m" : text

~ A `describe` group was entered, at `depth` (1 for an outermost group).
>> reportSuite = (name :: Text, depth :: Num) -> $ => print("`indent(depth - 1)``name`")

~ A case ran, at `depth`; `failed` says whether an `expect` in it failed.
>> reportCase = (name :: Text, depth :: Num, failed :: Bool) -> $ => <
  mark = failed ? red("✗") : green("✓")
  print("`indent(depth)``mark` `name`")
>

~ The run's total, and its status — non-zero when any case failed. The synthesized entry
~ point ends with this call, so what it returns is what the suite exits with.
>> reportSummary = () -> Num => <
  failed = casesFailed()
  tally = "`casesPassed()` passed, `failed` failed"
  print("")
  print(failed == 0 ? green(tally) : red(tally))
  failed == 0 ? 0 : 1
>

~ A group of cases, nestable. `body` runs immediately; the group is only there to name
~ and indent what it contains.
>> describe = (name :: Text, body :: () -> $) -> $ => <
  depth = enterSuite()
  reportSuite(name, depth)
  body()
  leaveSuite()
  $
>

~ One case, reported once `body` has run. A failing `expect` inside `body` marks the case
~ and skips what is left of it, so the report says which way the case went and the run
~ continues with the next one.
>> it = (name :: Text, body :: () -> $) -> $ => <
  body()
  failed = caseFailing()
  reportCase(name, finishCase(), failed)
>
